The HLE syscall sources and EeScheduler are compiled directly from the pinned
SDK checkout, with reproducible native-interface patches in patches/ps2recomp.
The previous locally derived kernel was removed in the maintainer-approved
migration of 2026-11-08. Context, checked guest memory, canonical clocks and
device transport adapters live in src/sdk_hle.cpp, src/sdk/ and the native
PS2Runtime backend. These adapters do not introduce another console runtime.
Unavailable interfaces refuse explicitly; this notice does not certify games.

Combined binaries linking this GPL component must be distributed under the
GPL-3.0 terms, with corresponding source and the applicable license notices.

SDK integration: ps2xAnalyzer and ps2xRecomp are built from the same pinned
PS2Recomp revision through cmake/PS2Recomp.cmake. Sources remain in the SDK
checkout (PS2N_PS2RECOMP_SOURCE_DIR); deps.lock.json records the revision,
transitive dependency revisions and reproducible patches in patches/ps2recomp.
Local changes: embeddable CMake paths, host-controlled compiler policy and
UTF-8 file paths, checked output writes and explicit error queries in the
recompiler. Upstream authorship/notices are preserved.
The SDK PS2Runtime class now has an exclusive integrated native backend,
implemented in src/ps2recomp_runtime.cpp, owning the platform CPU, Memory,
NVM and adapted HLE kernel. The standalone SDK memory, GS, scheduler and
VU/IOP interpreters are excluded from that backend. In the integrated output,
R5900Context aliases the existing execution context and the SDK emits constant
instructions through the platform native semantics. The standalone generated
ABI stays in a separate compilation profile. Remaining upstream services still
require adaptation.
SDK tools and combined binaries require
GPL-3.0 distribution terms and corresponding source, including these patches;
the original platform code retains its BSD-3-Clause notices. Dependencies
retain their own licenses and notices in their pinned source trees.

Native IOP reuse: ps2xIOP/src/emulator/services/iop_module_loader.cpp and
ps2xIOP/src/ps2_path.cpp are compiled from that same pinned SDK checkout.
The upstream emulator/core/iop_kernel.cpp and emulator/imports/iop_cdvd.cpp
are compiled against that adapter too; no IopCpuCore implementation is linked.
IopMemory allocation bookkeeping is adapted from emulator/core/iop_memory.cpp.
Patch 0006 selects iop_memory_native.hpp for the shared memory interface;
its ELF/IRX parsing and relocation implementation stays upstream. This
adapter borrows the existing Iop RAM and preserves its undefined-byte and
stopped-device refusals. No upstream IOP CPU, RAM or interpreter is linked.
